> The rooftop door sticks, and then gives, and then the whole sky is there.
> The rain has washed Mapo clean. The streets below are wet and orange. Above them, the kind of stars Seoul almost never lets you see.
> Someone drags up the blankets from the lobby. Someone else brings the cushions from Charlie's fort, which he insists on rebuilding at once.
@show charlie smile at=c
charlie: Fort two. Rooftop edition. Now with sky.
@hide all
@sfx step
> Twelve minutes later, Hyunjun and Justin come through the door with two bags each, out of breath.
> They are arguing about whether shrimp crackers are "a snack" or "a lifestyle."
> Right behind them, there is a knock on the rooftop door, and a delivery rider in a helmet holding a warm, heavy bag.
@show songha smile at=c
songha: Tteokbokki. From the twenty-four-hour place in Hapjeong. I ordered at 03:51.
@show daniel surprised at=r
daniel: You made a plan that *worked*?
songha: It's been a long night. I've been learning. I cut every step except the one that mattered.
@show charlie laugh at=l
charlie: Tteokbokki *and* convenience store! Both! Both is a food group! I said this hours ago!
@hide all
> It becomes a feast on a blanket: rice cakes too hot to eat, ramen going soft, kimbap, chips, a bag of tangerines nobody remembers buying.
@show hyunjun smile at=c
hyunjun: {{playerName}}. I got you something. Don't make it a thing.
@if var.snack == "kimbap"
    > A triangle kimbap. Tuna mayo. The correct answer, he told you hours ago, when you picked one out of his bag. He remembered.
@elif var.snack == "banana"
    > A carton of banana milk, straw already stuck to the side. The one you rescued from Justin, hours ago. He remembered.
@elif var.snack == "icecream"
    > An ice cream bar, a little soft from the run up the stairs. Rain or not, hours ago, that was your pick. He remembered.
@else
    > A little of everything, all in a pile, as if he couldn't decide and refused to have to.
hyunjun: It's a thing. I know. I made it a thing.
@hide all
@show hamin smile at=l
> Hamin sits down next to you and slides a can along the blanket until it touches your hand. He doesn't comment on it. He doesn't need to.
@show haruta smile at=r
haruta: Can I have the corner piece of tteokbokki? The burnt one. I want it. I'm saying that out loud.
@show daniel laugh at=c
daniel: Haruta wants something! Everybody, silence! Give the man the burnt one!
haruta[laugh]: You don't have to *announce* it.
