    @rel hanbi closeness+1
    @rel hamin closeness+1
    @rel haruta closeness+1
    @rel songha closeness+1
    > It takes a while. Nobody interrupts. When you reach the last one, Hanbi is smiling at his shoes.
@hide all
@music quiet
@amb wind
> After the food, the rooftop goes horizontal. Nine people lying on blankets, looking up, trading half-sentences with the sky.
> Charlie falls asleep for eleven minutes and wakes up in the middle of an argument about which constellation is shaped like a ladle.
> You get up to stretch. Somehow that turns into going round the roof, one person at a time.
@show hamin smile at=c
@cam closeup hamin
hamin: Are you cold?
you: A little.
hamin: Okay.
> He lifts one side of his coat, and waits. Not assuming. Just offering.
> You nod. He puts it round your shoulders and goes back to looking at the sky like nothing happened.
hamin: I didn't use to ask. I just used to move people out of the wind. I'm trying to ask now.
@hide all
@show haruta smile at=c
@cam closeup haruta
haruta: I've decided something. I'm staying up here until the power goes. Not because everyone is.
haruta: Because I want to. That's the whole reason. It's strange how good that feels to say.
you: Say it again.
haruta[laugh]: I want to. There. Twice in one night. Somebody should write it down.
@hide all
@show justin neutral at=c
@cam closeup justin
> Justin is sitting on the ledge-side bench, not dancing. His fingers tap on his knee: five, six, seven, eight.
justin: I'm not doing a bit, by the way. Right now. This is just me.
justin: It's quieter than I thought. Being just me. It's… okay, actually.
you: It suits you.
justin[smile]: Don't tell anyone. I have a reputation.
@hide all
@show songha smile at=c
@cam closeup songha
> Songha has put the notebook face down on the blanket. He points up at a star, very confidently.
songha: That one's called Gerald.
you: It is not called Gerald.
songha[laugh]: It is tonight. I've decided. No plan, no research. Just Gerald.
you: What's it really called?
songha: No idea. I'll look it up. Later. Not tonight.
@hide all
@show hanbi smile at=c
@cam closeup hanbi
> Hanbi turns his sketchbook round. Nine tiny figures on a rooftop. One of them is holding a can. One of them is pointing at a star named Gerald.
hanbi: It's rough. I'll fix the hands later.
hanbi: I'm glad you came tonight. {p}That's all. I wanted to say it out loud.
@hide all
@show hyunjun thinking at=c
@cam closeup hyunjun
hyunjun: I hate this part. The part where you can see the end coming.
hyunjun: But it's still happening. Right now. And after it's over, it'll still have happened. That's… that's something, right?
you: That's everything.
hyunjun[smile]: Okay. Yeah. I'm writing that on my hand.
@hide all
@show charlie smile at=c
@cam closeup charlie
charlie: Where are you going after this?
you: Home. I think. Wherever that is this month.
charlie: Wherever the snacks are. That's the rule. You made that one up, you know. Years ago.
charlie[laugh]: There are so many snacks up here. So technically you're home.
@hide all
@show daniel smile at=c
@cam closeup daniel
> Daniel is lying flat on his back with his arms spread out, doing nothing at all.
daniel: I haven't planned anything for the next ten minutes. No game. Nothing.
daniel: It's terrifying. It's fine. It's actually really fine.
> You lie down next to him. Neither of you says anything for a while. He doesn't fill it.
daniel: …Is this boring for you?
you: No.
daniel[smile]: Me neither. Weird. Good weird.
@hide all
@cam wide
@music quiet
> The sky goes from black to the deep blue that comes just before the deep blue that comes before morning.
> Across the rooftops, one window lights up. Someone else in Mapo is awake, making coffee, starting a day. It feels like being waved at.
> Justin and Hyunjun are sharing the last bag of shrimp crackers. Nobody is stealing. It is, as Hyunjun says, historic.
@show songha neutral at=l
songha: What's everyone doing tomorrow? Honestly. Not the schedule.
@show charlie thinking at=r
charlie: Sleeping until two. Then eating. Then sleeping.
@hide all
> Then it's your turn. You have moved house more times than you can count on both hands. You know exactly what you usually say next.
* [sincere] "I think I'm going to stay. In this city. For a while."
    @rel songha trust+1
    @rel hanbi trust+1
    @rel hyunjun trust+1
    @rel charlie trust+1
    > It's the first time you've said it out loud. It sounds truer outside your head than it did in it.
    songha[smile]: Then I'm adding you to the schedule. Permanently. You can't unsubscribe.
* [playful] "Unpacking. There are boxes in my room I've been ignoring for a month."
    @rel daniel closeness+1
    @rel justin closeness+1
    @rel charlie closeness+1
    daniel: We'll help. Nine people can unpack anything. We'll make it a game.
    justin: He will actually make it a game.
    you: …Then I guess I'm staying long enough to unpack.
* [quiet] "Maybe I'll stay." Say it quietly. Only the sky has to hear.
    @rel hamin trust+1
    @rel haruta trust+1
    @rel hanbi closeness+1
    > It isn't only the sky. Hamin hears it. You can tell because he doesn't turn his head, and because he smiles.
@hide all
@sfx chime
@textbox echo
echo: Recipients. It is almost 04:57.
echo: Please come down to the lobby. I have one question. And then I have to go.
@textbox normal
@show daniel neutral at=c
daniel: …Do we have to go down?
@show hanbi smile at=l
hanbi: We'll come back up. After. Come on.
@hide all
> Nine people fold up the blankets badly and go down the stairs together, slower than they need to.
@time 04:57
