=== friendship_ending
@chapter ending
@bg studio_lobby t=fade
@amb room
@music echo
@hide all
@cam wide
@textbox echo
echo: Tonight. All nine of you.
echo: I have checked. There is no record of tonight. Nobody submitted one. It has not had time to become old yet.
@textbox normal
@show daniel smile at=c
@if flag.group_photo
    > Daniel is already digging in his pocket. He pulls out a square of expired instant film, a little bent at one corner.
@else
    > Daniel is already digging through the front desk drawer, and comes up with the old instant camera and a single square of film.
daniel: Then here. Scan this. It's the only record we've got.
> He lays it on the glass of the terminal. Nine people, badly framed, laughing at something none of them can remember.
@sfx echo
@fx memory n=1
@textbox echo
echo: …Oh.
echo: RECORD 10. TYPE: PHOTOGRAPH. DATE: TONIGHT.
echo: OWNERS: HANBI. HAMIN. SONGHA. CHARLIE. HYUNJUN. HARUTA. JUSTIN. DANIEL. {{playerName}}.
echo: UNRESOLVED SUBJECTS: 0.
echo: For six years, every record I kept had someone missing from it. Someone I could not name.
echo: This one has nobody missing. I did not know a record could look like this.
@textbox normal
> In the terminal's slot, a card of glass begins to glow. The photograph surfaces inside it slowly, like something rising through water.
> It comes out warm. Somehow it comes out warm.
@hide all
@show hyunjun sad at=r
hyunjun: I said I'd cry at it. I'm crying at it. Nobody look at me.
@show justin smile at=l
justin: Everyone's looking at you.
hyunjun[laugh]: I know! It's fine! It's a happy one!
@hide all
@show charlie thinking at=c
charlie: Okay, but who keeps it? There's one card. There are nine of us.
@show songha thinking at=l
songha: A rotation. A week each. And before anyone says no—
> Nobody says no. For the first time all night, nobody says no to the schedule.
songha[surprised]: …Oh. Okay. Wow. It feels different when people agree.
@show charlie smile at=r
charlie: {{playerName}} goes first.
charlie: You're the one who always leaves, right? So if you have it, you have to come back. To hand it over. That's the rule.
@hide all
> Eight people look at you. Nobody is teasing. It's the way people look at someone when they're handing them something that matters.
* [sincere] "Then I'll come back. That's a promise."
    @rel charlie trust+1
    @rel songha trust+1
    charlie[laugh]: It's in the schedule now. Songha wrote it down. It's legally binding.
* [playful] "One week, and then I'm fighting Songha for a second week."
    @rel songha closeness+1
    @rel daniel closeness+1
    songha[laugh]: I'll allow one appeal.
* [quiet] Take the card in both hands, and hold it like it might still be warm tomorrow.
    @rel hanbi closeness+1
    @rel hamin closeness+1
    > It is. You don't know that yet. But it is.
@hide all
> The Archive Wall has begun to dim, box by box, from the top down. Nobody needs to be told what that means.
@show justin smile at=l
justin: Thanks for keeping my stuff, ECHO. Even the embarrassing stuff.
@show haruta smile at=r
haruta: Thank you. Really. It was a good screening.
@show hyunjun sad at=c
hyunjun: Sleep well, okay? You earned it. Best building ever.
@hide all
@show hamin neutral at=c
hamin: You kept the light on for a long time. Somebody should notice that. {p}We noticed.
@hide all
@call echo_farewell
@time 05:40
@bg dawn_rooftop t=slow d=2.4
@amb birds
@fx light n=0.8
@music dawn
@cam reveal
> Afterwards, without the lights, the building is just a building. You climb the stairs by phone torch, all nine of you, back to the roof.
> The sky over Mapo has gone the colour of peach tea left out overnight. Somewhere, a bus is starting its first route.
@show charlie sad at=c
charlie: My phone's dead. Again. Does anyone—
> Hanbi hands him the battery pack without looking. The battery pack does a full lap of the roof before it comes back to him, with a little less charge.
@hide all
@show songha smile at=l
songha: New schedule. Nothing until noon. That's it. That's the whole schedule.
@show justin laugh at=r
justin: Best schedule you've ever made.
songha[laugh]: I know. I'm framing it.
@hide all
@show daniel laugh at=c
daniel: Numbers! Everyone! I'm making a group chat. It's called "Stuck-in-a-Talking-Building Friends."
@show charlie laugh at=r
charlie: I'm renaming it "Ghost and Eight Others."
@show songha smile at=l
songha: I'm pinning a schedule to it. Don't mute it.
@hide all
@sfx phone
> Your phone buzzes once. Then eight more times, in a row, like a small applause.
> Nine names in a list. You have never been in a group chat you didn't leave within a year. You look at this one for a long moment.
> Then, one at a time, they take your phone and save themselves into it properly.
> Songha saves himself as "Songha (schedule)." Daniel saves himself as "Daniel ★ Leader ★" and Justin changes it to "Daniel" before the phone comes back.
> Hanbi's contact has no note at all. Just his name, and a small drawing of a pencil where the photo would go.
@show charlie laugh at=c
charlie: I saved myself as "Charlie (youngest, not my fault)." For legal reasons.
@cg cg_friendship
@unlock cg:cg_friendship
@music credits
> The sun comes up over the rooftops of Mapo.
> Nine people stand at the edge of a building that won't exist next week, squinting at it like it's the first sunrise ever made.
> Nobody says anything clever. Hyunjun is still crying a bit. Justin is doing one slow, silly spin. Haruta is humming something that isn't from any film.
@cg off
@show haruta smile at=l
haruta: That would be a good last shot. If this were a film.
@show hamin smile at=r
hamin: It isn't the last one, though.
haruta[laugh]: No. It isn't.
@hide all
> The glass card is in your coat pocket. You keep touching it, the way you check for keys. It is still, somehow, a little warm.
@sfx step
> Down in the alley, a van pulls up. Renovation crew. It's time to go.
@show hyunjun smile at=l
hyunjun: Breakfast? Right now? There's a place by the station that does—
@show songha laugh at=r
songha: Next week. It's on the schedule. Go home, sleep.
hyunjun[laugh]: Next week, then. I'm holding everyone to it. I'm writing it on my other hand.
@show charlie smile at=c
charlie: I'm sleeping until two. Nobody text me until two. Actually, text me. I want the texts.
@hide all
@show hanbi smile at=c
hanbi: {{playerName}}. See you.
> He says it the way people say it when they mean the next time is already real. Not a door closing. A door propped open with a shoe.
* [sincere] "See you. I mean it."
    @rel hanbi trust+1
    hanbi: I know. I can tell.
* [playful] "See you next week. It's on Songha's schedule."
    @rel songha closeness+1
    songha: Finally. Someone who reads the schedule.
* [quiet] Hold up the glass card, just a little. Proof.
    @rel hanbi closeness+1
    hanbi[smile]: …Yeah. See you.
@hide all
> And then it's everyone at once, overlapping, on the stairs, in the alley, under the laundromat's light.
@show hamin smile at=l
hamin: Text when you get home. So we know.
@show haruta smile at=r
haruta: See you, {{playerName}}. Next week. I'll pick the film, if we watch one. I already know which.
@show daniel laugh at=c
daniel: See you! See you! I'm saying it twice so it counts double!
@hide all
> You have always been the one who leaves. You're leaving now, down the stairs, past the laundromat, out into the morning.
> But it's different. You know exactly where you're coming back to.
@ending friendship
@credits
@end

