@chapter newmem
@bg dawn_cafe tint=night t=fade
@amb cafe
@music fun
@hide all
@cam wide
> A week later. A tteokbokki place two streets over from where Studio 25 used to be. It's loud, it's steaming, and it closes at midnight. Songha has checked.
@show songha neutral at=l
songha: We booked for seven. It's seven-twenty. Where's Hyunjun?
@show daniel laugh at=r
daniel: He texted "one more stop" forty minutes ago. That's all. Just "one more stop."
@hide all
@show hanbi neutral at=c
hanbi: He's fine. He shared his location. He's… walking in circles near the station.
songha: That's not fine. That's Hyunjun.
@hide all
@sfx bell
@show hyunjun laugh at=c
hyunjun: I'm here! I got off one stop early to walk past the old building. It's all scaffolding now. It looks like it's wearing a jacket.
@show justin smile at=r
> Justin takes a fish cake off Hyunjun's plate before he has even sat down.
hyunjun: You didn't even wait for me to sit!
justin: I waited a week.
@hide all
@show haruta smile at=l
haruta: I'll order. The cheese one, extra rice cakes. I want the cheese one. I decided on the train.
@show daniel surprised at=r
daniel: Haruta ordered for the table! Everyone, a round of applause!
haruta[laugh]: Please don't clap. The whole restaurant is looking.
@hide all
@show charlie thinking at=c
charlie: Wait, what's happening? Why is everyone clapping?
all: Sit down, Charlie.
@hide all
@show hamin smile at=c
@if var.drink == "peach"
    > Hamin slides a peach iced tea across the table to you without a word. The restaurant doesn't even sell peach iced tea. He must have brought it.
@elif var.drink == "choco"
    > Hamin slides a hot chocolate across the table to you without a word. The restaurant doesn't even sell hot chocolate. He must have brought it.
@elif var.drink == "grape"
    > Hamin slides a grape soda across the table to you without a word. The restaurant doesn't even sell grape soda. He must have brought it.
@else
    > Hamin slides a black coffee across the table to you without a word. The restaurant doesn't even sell coffee. He must have brought it.
hamin: You were going to forget to drink anything. You always do when it's loud.
@hide all
@show hanbi smile at=l
> Hanbi's phone is at ninety-four percent. Everyone else's is under twenty. He puts the charger in the middle of the table like a centrepiece.
@show songha smile at=r
songha: Okay. Agenda. Item one: whose week is it with the card?
> Everyone looks at you. The glass card is in your coat pocket. You checked for it three times on the way here.
you: Mine. Still mine. It's been one week exactly.
songha[laugh]: Then you have to hand it over. That was the rule.
@hide all
> You put it on the table between the tteokbokki and the charger. Nine people, badly framed, laughing, catching the restaurant light.
@show daniel smile at=c
daniel: New rule. Whoever has it next has to host. Which means another dinner. Which means next week. Which means—
@show charlie laugh at=r
charlie: Which means we just keep doing this forever?
daniel: Exactly. That's the whole plan.
@hide all
> By the door, Daniel has found a claw machine the size of a fridge. He has already spent four thousand won on it.
@show daniel laugh at=r
daniel: It's a different claw machine. It's a *new* claw machine. The old grudge doesn't apply.
@show justin smile at=l
justin: You've lost five times.
daniel: Five times to a *new* machine. That's a fresh start.
@hide all
> The food arrives, too hot and too much. Somebody knocks over a cup. Somebody starts laughing and can't stop.
> It isn't a memory yet. It's just Tuesday. You stay until they close.
@end
